cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CUNEUS: optics-aware data formats for archival storage in glass"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24325754
authors:
  - family-names: Guettal
    given-names: Hakim
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GuettHM/cuneus"
url: "https://guetthm.github.io/cuneus/"
abstract: >-
  Open simulator for a concept of archival optical data storage in glass in which
  the storage format (lattice, symbol alphabet, decoder) is computed from the
  optics of the reader. Phase 1 compares square and hexagonal lattices of
  amplitude/phase dots read by coherent imaging, with a linear equaliser and with
  interference cancellation, a response learnt from known symbols, dot placement
  errors and defocus. Successor of 4D-VODS (doi:10.5281/zenodo.24268721).
  The author is not a professional physicist; the study was built with the help
  of AI tools on standard diffraction optics.
keywords:
  - optical data storage
  - archival storage
  - glass
  - hexagonal lattice
  - equalisation
  - interference cancellation
  - simulation
references:
  - type: software
    title: "4D-VODS: optical data storage in glass with a self-aligning code for low-cost readers"
    authors:
      - family-names: Guettal
        given-names: Hakim
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24268721
